-- title:
--   Multiplying by xⱼ^k makes a twist section polynomial
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $n$ a natural number, $Z$ a scheme and $\iota : Z \to \mathrm{Proj}\,A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ (the $\mathrm{Proj}$ of the graded ring given by the homogeneous submodules of `MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) A`) a closed immersion; write $\pi$ for the structure morphism $\iota$ followed by `ProjSpace.π A n` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and for each $i$ let `ProjSpace.pullbackChart ι i` be the open $\iota^{-1}D_+(x_i) \subseteq Z$. Fix $e \in \mathbb{N}$ and an element $m$ of `ProjSpace.twistFam`, i.e. a family assigning to each $d \in \mathbb{Z}$ and each $i \in \{0,\dots,n\}$ a section of $\mathcal{O}_Z$ over $\top \sqcap \iota^{-1}D_+(x_i)$, and assume $m$ lies in the degree-$e$ piece of the graded module `ProjSpace.twistGradedModule`: $m\,d' = 0$ for $d' \neq e$ and the family $m\,e$ satisfies the compatibility predicate `TwistCompat` for $\iota$ in degree $e$ over $\top$. Fix $j$. Then there are $k \in \mathbb{N}$ and $F \in A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ homogeneous of degree $e+k$ such that for every $i$ the $i$-th component in degree $e+k$ of the $k$-fold iterate of the operator `xMul j` (which sends a family $f$ to $d, i \mapsto$ the restriction of the frame unit `frameUnit ι i j` times $f(d-1)\,i$) applied to $m$ equals the restriction to $\top \sqcap \iota^{-1}D_+(x_i)$ of the image under $\iota$ on sections over $D_+(x_i)$ of the section `Proj.awayToSection` attached to the homogeneous localisation $F/x_i^{\,e+k}$ of degree $e+k$.
--
--   This is the saturation step in the identification of the twisted section module of a closed subscheme $Z \subseteq \mathbb{P}^n_A$ with a graded module generated by polynomials: a compatible family of degree $e$ becomes, after multiplication by a sufficiently high power of $x_j$, globally given by a single homogeneous polynomial divided by $x_i^{\,e+k}$ on each standard chart. It is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.exists_forall_mem_grade_exists_isHomogeneous_forall_apply_eq_of_isClosedImmersion`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.exists_forall_mem_grade_exists_isHomogeneous_forall_apply_eq_of_isClosedImmersion), where the power is made uniform over the charts.
